                <pb facs="0512" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/311: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Marseille</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-29T20:00:00-05:00">March 29, 1937—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 29th, arrest volunteers. Take up passports and request applicants furnish
                    names and addresses of persons who will supply funds for maintenance and return
                    United States. Cable result interview, including French position in the
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
